From 60d36a68a376bd4e236cf9850e7747adfff620db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Horizon authors <>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:18:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Memory: code that only an overlay calls moves into it (the VS
 mode's combat and intro to VS, the battle UI to BTL, the movie decoder and CD
 streaming to MOV); library functions nothing calls are dropped by the link:
 46.6 KB more heap in every build

docs/mods/memory.md "Code out of the executable". No C file changes:
- mk/version/us.mk: the Psy-Q code is one section per function (glabel already opens .text.NAME), except libapi,
  libgte and libmcrd (code copied by address range, functions that fall through); --gc-sections drops the 27
  functions nothing references (libgpu 7272 bytes, libsnd 740, libspu 572, libcd 240, libpress 144).
- config/us/overlay.ld, main.ld: src/vs/vs_combat.c and vs_intro.c (code, rodata) at the end of VS (+21196);
  src/main/battle_ui.c at the end of BTL (+5732); libpress, its tables and libcd's streaming functions (St*,
  CdRead2, the ring callbacks, which MOV_playMovie unhooks before it returns) and SetDefDispEnv at the end of MOV
  (+10728). tools/xref.py found them: nothing in the executable references them, only that overlay calls them.
  Every overlay address stays where it was. Link asserts: BTL and VS end at or below STD's end, MOV below TRN's slot.
- mk/platform/psx.mk: --emit-relocs, for tools/xref.py; the executable and overlays are the same bytes.
main_BSS_END (US text, 0x18800): integration 0x801CB574 -> 0x801BFF40 (heap over MIN_HEAP 37 260 -> 83 904; with the
Makefile's 0x20000: 6 540 -> 53 184); tier 2 0x801D4810 -> 0x801C91EC (752 -> 47 380 on 2 MB).

